Conservation Renewal Agenda

v0.4.4 — ESA Species Outcomes: Performance Analysis Framework

Status

Working analytical artifact | Wildlife & Biodiversity Pillar

1. Purpose

This document converts the FY2021–FY2022 U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service (FWS) recovery report into a performance-analysis framework for the American Conservation Renewal project.

The objective is not to produce a simplistic verdict on the Endangered Species Act (ESA). Instead, the analysis asks how effectively the national conservation system moves species through the sequence:

Early warning → Prevention → Stabilization → Improvement → Downlisting → Recovery → Delisting → Persistence

The FWS report provides a strong starting point because it presents species-level information on listing status, recovery plans, implemented recovery actions, five-year status reviews, and status-review recommendations for the 1,589 domestic listed species under FWS lead responsibility at the end of FY2022.

2. Quantitative Baseline

At the close of FY2022, FWS had lead responsibility for:

1,589 federally listed domestic species

1,236 endangered species

353 threatened species

1,248 species (79%) with recovery plans

1,484 species listed for at least five years with completed status reviews (95%)

